@page "/awards"
@page "/Awards.aspx"

<PageTitle>Awards</PageTitle>

<section class="page-section narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Awards</p>
    <h1>Recognition earned over years of storm tracking software.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The original awards page was a wall of proof: editorial quotes, product badges, ratings, and user feedback showing how strongly Tracking The Eye resonated with weather watchers.</p>
</section>

<section class="quote-grid award-grid">
    <article class="quote-card">
        <p class="card-kicker">PC Computing</p>
        <img class="award-badge" src="/images/1001.gif" alt="PC Computing Best of the Net badge" />
        <blockquote>"It's more fun and a lot more informative than those fake disasters on the movie screen this summer."</blockquote>
        <p class="quote-source">Voted Best Of The Net.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="quote-card">
        <p class="card-kicker">MSNBC The Site</p>
        <div class="award-strip">
            <img src="/images/thesite1.gif" alt="The Site logo 1" />
            <img src="/images/thesite2.gif" alt="The Site logo 2" />
            <img src="/images/thesite3.gif" alt="The Site logo 3" />
        </div>
        <blockquote>Picked as Shareware o' the Day on 6/11/97.</blockquote>
        <p class="quote-source">A headline callout on the original site.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="quote-card">
        <p class="card-kicker">Preston Gralla, Ziff-Davis</p>
        <img class="award-inline" src="/images/preston.gif" alt="Preston Gralla" />
        <blockquote>"If you'd like use the Internet to track the progress of hurricanes, check out Tracking the Eye."</blockquote>
        <p class="quote-source">The full review highlighted real-time storm coordinates, outlooks, advisories, forecasts, a full-color map, animation, and hurricane sound effects.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="quote-card">
        <p class="card-kicker">ZDNet and Users</p>
        <img class="award-inline wide-inline" src="/images/zd5star.gif" alt="ZDNet five-star rating" />
        <blockquote>"TTE is the slickest, funnest weather program I have ever downloaded."</blockquote>
        <p class="quote-source">Long-time customers and software reviewers both pushed the product toward five-star credibility.</p>
    </article>
</section>
